    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nMoved every date-derived owner value onto a **fiscal-year basis** (fiscal year runs 1 July\u201330 June, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 so a registration date on/after 1 July belongs to the fiscal year ending the following June).\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/FiscalYear.java`:\n- `endingYearOf(date)` \u2014 the year the fiscal year ends in\n- `labelOf(date)` \u2192 `FY<YY>` (null-safe)\n- `elapsedYears(from, to)` \u2014 whole elapsed fiscal years\n\n**Changes to existing behaviour:**\n1. **`fiscalYear` (new field)** \u2014 added to the `OwnerDto` schema in `openapi.yml` and wired in `OwnerMapper` as `FiscalYear.labelOf(owner.getRegistrationDate())`, derived from the business-day-adjusted registration date. Returned as `FY<YY>`.\n2. **Membership identifier** \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber` now takes its `M<YY>` year segment from the registration date's *fiscal* year instead of the calendar year.\n3. **Tenure** \u2014 `MembershipLevel` now scores the tenure point on **elapsed fiscal years \u2265 1** (a 1 July boundary crossed since registration) rather than a 365-day window. A newly-created owner still has zero tenure, so the \"never reaches level 4 at creation\" invariant holds.\n\nDescriptions in `openapi.yml` for `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` were updated to match.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit log confirms consistency for a today-dated (2026-08-17) owner: `membershipNumber=NSW-...-M27`, i.e. August 2026 \u2192 fiscal year FY27, and the new `fiscalYear` field matches the `FY\\d{2}` contract the test asserts.",
